  <page_number>30</page_number>
  <running_head>P. Rami</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>varia-</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">rundo : aliquando etiam commune, ut</l>
    <l n="2">ὁ χὴ γέϱανος grus, ὁ χὴ χὼ anser.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Communiter masculina, Atticé</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>faminina sunt, ut</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">ἀσϐολος fuligo,</l>
    <l n="6">ὕαλος vitrum,</l>
    <l n="7">ςρύχος solanum herba,</l>
    <l n="8">ϙόλος tholus, testudo ædificii.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Communiter fœminina, Attice</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>masculina sunt,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">λιμὸς fames,</l>
    <l n="12">χοῖς terra aggesta,</l>
    <l n="13">ῆς acervus, litus.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>Communiter masculina, Ionicé</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>fœmina sunt,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">ἔλλὸς cervus,</l>
    <l n="17">ἡμίονος mulus,</l>
    <l n="18">χίων columna,</l>
    <l n="19">χύων canis,</l>
    <l n="20">βοῦς bos,</l>
    <l n="21">βῶλος gleba. Itaque genus pro dialecto varia-</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Greek words are printed with accents and breathings that are partly blurred in the scan; the Greek is transcribed as far as legible. Some Greek forms (e.g. ὁ χὴ, ςρύχος, ϙόλος) are doubtful.</notes>
